# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads as the build context.
#
# THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING, AND ITS ABSENCE IS A SILENT FAILURE. With no
# .gcloudignore, gcloud synthesises the ignore list from .gitignore — and
# .gitignore deliberately excludes web/data/*.bin, because the solved fields are
# 189 MB of build output that has no business in a git repository. The container
# reads those files at startup and cannot rebuild them. So the default behaviour
# uploads an application with its model removed, the image builds cleanly, and
# the server answers 503 on every request that needs data.
#
# The rule to remember: .gitignore answers "what is not source?" and this file
# answers "what does the server not need?" Those are different questions, and
# web/data is the case where they give opposite answers.

.git/
.gitignore

# The pipeline's raw inputs — LiDAR tiles, NYC footprints, cached FortyGuard
# responses and the credit ledger. Only `cli build` reads them, and that never
# runs in the image.
data/

.env
node_modules/

tests/
test-results/
playwright-report/
notebooks/
*.ipynb

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Agent run transcripts are per-machine scratch, except the one the film replays.
.agent/runs/*
!.agent/runs/r17880442193644fa/

Design Overhaul Request.zip
*:Zone.Identifier
.deploy/
